ey in those installments parker says  he was fired after taking an approved  vacation i was devastated i loved that  company i'd worked very hard for them i  couldn't believe they had done this to  me  devastated he says he hopes the lawsuit  proves no employee is too small in that  business owners particularly in the  restaurant industry will be held  accountable i'm hoping  to show them that i can lead by example  and if you guys have problems with  employers don't be afraid to speak up  you're not alone out there  now the good news is police did find the  robber charging him for a string of  incidents across the valley the state  labor commission facilitated a  settlement with parker and the lodge for  55-hundred dollars which his lawyers say  he did not accept we did reach out to  the lodge and did not hear back i'm  david charns live local now
 

